  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC phase-out Management Plan (Stage II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the HPMP Stage II remains to reflect the commitment of Brunei to its obligation as a Party to the Montreal Protocol having in mind the socio-economic needs of the country. Under the HPMP Stage II, it aims to assist Brunei to achieve a complete phase out of HCFC by 2030 with 2.5% servicing tail for 2030 to 2040.  Brunei#s consumption of HCFC remains only in the servicing of refrigeration and air-conditioning (RAC) equipment. To reduce consumpt ion and curb the growth of HCFCs, four project activities have been identified and introduced under the HPMP Stage II, including Activity 1) Policy, regulations and enforcement amendments and activities; Activity 2) RAC technician training and certification; Activ ity 3) Public awareness and outreach; and Activity 4) Implementation, Coordination and Monitoring.  HPMP Stage II was approved in principle at the 86th ExCom meeting that UNEP was the leading implementation agency and UNDP was the cooperating implementation agency. At 91st ExCom meeting, it was further approved that the cooperating implementation agency was changed from UNDP to UNIDO, and funds (US $234,000, plus agency support costs of US $21,060) were transferred from UNDP to UNIDO. The first tranche and corresponding implementation plans were also approved at 91st ExCom meeting in the amount o</narrative>
  </description>
